Task 3: Protected Route and Dashboard (20 points)

Build a ProtectedRoute component and a Dashboard page:

ProtectedRoute:

    Wraps any component that requires authentication
    Checks if a user is logged in (via AuthContext)
    Checks if the JWT token is expired by decoding it and comparing the exp field to the current time
    If not authenticated or token is expired: redirect to the login form and clear localStorage
    If authenticated: render the wrapped component

jsx
Copy

function ProtectedRoute({ children }) {
  const { user } = useAuth();
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');

  // Check if token exists and is not expired
  if (!user || !token) {
    return <Navigate to login />;
  }

  // Decode token and check expiry (without verifying signature)
  // jwt tokens are base64: JSON.parse(atob(token.split('.')[1]))
  const payload = JSON.parse(atob(token.split('.')[1]));
  if (payload.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) {
    // Token expired -- clear storage, redirect
  }

  return children;
}

Dashboard:

    Displays the authenticated user's information: name, email, and member since date
    Shows a "Log Out" button that calls the logout function from AuthContext
    Fetches fresh user data from GET /api/auth/me on mount (using the stored token in the Authorization header)
    After logout, the user is redirected back to the login form

Expected output: The dashboard shows user info and is only accessible with a valid token. Clicking logout clears the token and returns to login. Visiting the dashboard URL directly without a token redirects to login.
